    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-76506",
      "publishedDate": "2026-11-04T16:27:03.469Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-11-04T16:27:03.469Z",
      "description": "A vulnerability in the web-based management interface of Cisco UCS Central Software could allow an authenticated, remote attacker to achieve remote code execution or conduct information disclosure attacks on an affected device.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to insufficient validation of user-supplied input in an HTTP request. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected endpoint on an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to execute arbitrary commands, write arbitrary files to the filesystem, and obtain sensitive information. To exploit this vulnerability, the attacker must have valid user credentials on the affected device.\r\nCisco has released software updates that address this vulnerability There are no workarounds that address this vulnerability.",
      "severity": 7.6,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Cisco Cisco Unified Computing System Central Software\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
